      <h2>Beyond relocating top-down services</h2>
      <p>
        The national transition towards neighbourhood health is the right instinct &mdash; but it must amount to more than simply relocating top-down clinical services into community venues. The defining opportunity is to give neighbourhood health real purpose: <strong>health creation, led by places and communities.</strong>
      </p>

      <img src="assets/images/feature-walking.jpeg" alt="Neighbourhood walking and community health" style="width:100%;">

      <h2>The Pillars of Authentic Neighbourhood health</h2>
      <div class="policy-step">
        <div class="policy-step-number">&bull;</div>
        <div class="policy-step-body">
          <h4>Relational Capacity</h4>
          <p>Prioritising human relationships, trusted community champions, and peer networks that build genuine confidence and resilience.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-step">
        <div class="policy-step-number">&bull;</div>
        <div class="policy-step-body">
          <h4>Shared Community Delivery</h4>
          <p>Co-designing services with residents, faith groups, sports clubs, and cultural anchors rather than imposing rigid institutional models.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-step">
        <div class="policy-step-number">&bull;</div>
        <div class="policy-step-body">
          <h4>Strengthening Human Connection</h4>
          <p>Deploying digital tools that support human relationships and community connection rather than replacing them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

